Description: Runs language model agents in an existing 'R' session, where
    generated code can inspect and modify objects already in memory. The
    peter() function supports interactive chat and programmatic calls.
    Conversational models use tools and return session objects; typed
    decision models return logical, character or numeric vectors with
    associated model probabilities. Supports the 'Anthropic'
    <https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/overview>, 'OpenAI'
    <https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/overview> and 'Google Gemini'
    <https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs> APIs, 'OpenAI'-compatible endpoints,
    local 'Ollama' <https://ollama.com> models, and the 'Claude Code' and
    'Codex' command line tools. Decision models include 'Jev', hosted by
    'TypeSafe AI' <https://docs.typesafe.ai/introduction>, and the local 'Clef'.
    Top-level agent calls and their executed code can be recorded in 'R'
    scripts, 'R Markdown' and 'Quarto' documents, or 'Jupyter' notebooks.
    Recorded 'R' scripts can be replayed without model calls when the required
    inputs and packages are available.
